sweeps.method:
1) Tighten the shared identity test in hoursSweep's mentionsShop:
- match the name as a whole word, never as a substring of a domain;
- drop the town-only fallback;
- generic names such as 'Tobacco Store' pass only when the domain is the name;
- add local.yahoo.com, exxonmobilfuels.com, usps.com and wikipedia.org to NOT_THE_SHOPS_SITE.
2) Refuse at decide time:
- another listing's town or a brand-plus-town heading between the address and the hours;
- blocks labelled casino, convenience store, mall or '<town> hours';
- weekday-only 8-5 or 9-5 blocks near support, office, fax, orders or example.com.
3) Parser fixes:
- read every comma range;
- a leading 00:00-04:00 segment is the previous night;
- accept 25:00-28:00;
- '12: 00' reads as '12:00';
- '4 pm - 12 pm' means midnight;
- a day 12 hours off the others, or shorter than 2 hours, becomes unknown and goes to review.
4) Parse season windows into hours_valid_from and hours_valid_until, and refuse a schedule whose window excludes today.
5) Re-run decide on the saved evidence for all 1,077. Review every schedule that would now be refused or changed. Clear or replace only the confirmed ones.

