sweeps.method:
1) Pull the WPSL feeds with a radius grid until no new ids appear. Keep a feed only if at least 80% of its names carry the brand (this rejects JO's stockist list).
2) Match by phone within 30 mi, addressKey plus ZIP/town, or house number plus ZIP near OUR pin. Never use feed coordinates alone: 4 of 4 checked disagreements had the feed pin wrong.
3) Decisions:
- rename on a phone match, keeping the old name as an alias;
- keep the row whose address equals the feed and hide the others as duplicates, exempting the in-store lounges;
- fill feed hours;
- set has_lounge on the 19 lounge addresses;
- clear links to the old brand or the chain host on unlisted rows and queue them for closure review. Never hide on absence alone.
4) Missing branches: require a live store page with hours and an independent Census geocode within 0.5 mi. Insert with source='chain', or fill an existing OSM stub.
5) Re-pull monthly. A chain row missing from two pulls goes to the closure queue.

Fetch the homepage and contact page, and capture title, og:site_name, logo alt, JSON-LD name, address and telephone, tel: links and footer text.
Pass if a distinctive name token appears, or our phone, or our street number plus street and town. A host-venue pass covers casino, hotel and restaurant lounges that show our address or phone.
